  (text "R4 with C3: 720 Hz\nbass passes at unity below it" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 116.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "138cc8a7-b4dc-5063-9793-ae8fc4403800"))
  (text "C4 with Rf: 61.2 kHz (Drive 0)\nto 5.66 kHz (Drive 100)\nG = 1 + Rf/R4 = 11.9 to 118\nRf = R6 + RVX1" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 132.08 104.14 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7f13f5e7-63d5-5488-bdda-0ed88ac0a6b1"))
  (text "Sections 4 and 5 of the circuit notes: a non-inverting stage, G = 1 + Zf/Zg, values confirmed in [2].\nUX1: modelled as an ideal op-amp. DX1, DX2: two silicon diodes in anti-parallel across the feedback [3];\nthe DSP limits the feedback branch voltage with a soft knee at 0.6 V (Vd reported [2], knee shape chosen).\nRVX1: the 500 kOhm Drive pot [2] with a log law, about 9 % at noon (chosen; no source gives the taper).\nIn the DSP the C4 low-pass comes before the diodes; in this circuit they share a node (section 5)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 198.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0e8fd369-ec9f-5dc2-aa1b-0a37642e0414"))
